<title>USA: N.Y. business loans rose $336 mln August 21 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans rose $336 mln August 21 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the seven major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $336 million to $41,061 million in the week ended August 21, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $337 million to $41,290 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $6.754 billion to $735,075 million.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
